    "title": "HP Bleed Air Systems - Unpressurized Configuration",
    "category": "C",
    "numberInstalled": 2,
    "numberRequired": 0,
    "oProcedure": "36-01-02: ER operations are not permitted with an inoperative Bleed Air System. Flightcrew will ensure: 1. Airplane is not operated in known or forecast icing conditions, 2. Rear baggage compartment is not used, 3. Internal baggage door remains OPEN, and 4. Airplane is operated in accordance with AFM Chapter 1, Limitations. To operate the airplane unpressurized: 1. Select manual pressurization and 2. Slew the outflow valve to the full open position with RAM Air selected ON. 3. Monitor cabin differential pressure to be nominally zero psid during the flight.",
    "mProcedure": "36-01-02: Ensure inoperative Bleed Air Valve is CLOSED and deactivated electrically.",
    "placardLocation": "Adjacent To The Associated Bleed Air Control Switch",
    "provisos": "(M)(O) Except for ER operations, may be inoperative provided: a) Inoperative Bleed Control Valve is CLOSED and deactivated electrically when associated Engine Bleed Air System is selected OFF, b) Airplane is not operated in forecast or known icing conditions, c) Rear baggage compartment is not used (empty), d) Internal baggage door remains OPEN, and e) Airplane is operated in accordance with AFM Limitations."
