    "oProcedure": "Flightcrew will ensure: 1. With the parking brake applied and the Main Door closed, the Main Door is visually confirmed latched and locked, and 2. On line up and ready with power levers advanced to takeoff power for takeoff, reconfirm the correct position of the following: A. FLAP Handle, B. SPEED BRAKE Handle, C. PARK/EMERGE BRAKE Handle, D. Landing Gear Control Handle, E. Thrust Reverser Levers, F. GPWS/GND SPLR FLAP ORIDE Switch, and G. Pitch, Rudder, and/or Roll Trim.",
    "placardLocation": "Adjacent To The Main Entry Door Warning Indication",
    "provisos": "(O) May be inoperative provided: a) With the parking brake applied and the Main Door closed, the Main Door is visually confirmed latched and locked, b) On line up and ready with power levers advanced to takeoff power for takeoff, reconfirm the correct position of the following: 1. FLAP Handle, 2. SPEED BRAKE Handle, 3. PARK/EMERG BRAKE Handle, 4. Landing Gear Control Handle, 5. Thrust Reverser Levers, 6. GPWS/GND SPLR FLAP ORIDE Switch, 7. Pitch, Rudder, and/or Roll Trim, and c) Repairs are made within 1 flight-day. NOTE: \"Main Door\" Blue Advisory CAS Message will change to an Amber Caution CAS Message once the parking brake is released. In addition, it will trigger an associated red \"Aircraft Configuration\" Warning CAS Message when thrust levers are advanced to takeoff power. This warning cannot be inhibited and must be acknowledged.",
